@@ -9,6 +9,17 @@ pnpm install && pnpm run start
 
 The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 
+Client-side navigation retains the five most recently visited views (including
+the active view). Returning to a retained route reuses its DOM, form state, and
+event listeners. Inactive views use `content-visibility: hidden` and are inert;
+older views are evicted in least-recently-used order. Paths and query strings
+identify views, while fragments share a view. Astro still fetches destinations
+and manages metadata, scripts, history, and scroll restoration. Navigating to the
+current route or reloading refreshes its content and state.
+
+Run `pnpm test` for the automated DOM cache checks and `pnpm build` for the
+production build.
+
 ## Tech Stack
 
 - **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
